2. Symlink chain fixture contradicts the stated algorithm. §7 says canonicalize happens first; A→B→outside returns `OutsideWorkspace` before open. The fixture expects `SymlinkRefused` at A via `O_NOFOLLOW`, which cannot happen after canonicalizing to the outside target. Lines 31-32, 153-160, 187.

3. CI lint gate is unscoped/unimplementable as written. A repo-wide forbid on `std::fs::read*`, `metadata`, `read_dir`, `OpenOptions`, etc. will trip many existing non-ingestion callsites; if the intended boundary is W2 ingestion reads only, the packet must specify scan scope and exceptions. Lines 191-196, 210-211.

4. Reserved-name slug coverage is internally inconsistent. §2 says Windows reserved names as `register_other` slug reject; §8 tests `"CON"` while saying the regex accepts it, but the regex rejects uppercase. Lowercase `"con"` still passes, and Windows validation is deferred. Lines 30, 59, 140, 223.

Substrate check: `CategoryNotAllowed`/`RegisterError` have no current code collision; `StartRunSeed` is not in this W1-B packet, only W1-C.

